🚽 Regression for issue 246 (formerly return_from_inside_loop_in_main_fail):
🚽 `bussin` inside a loop in skibidi main must terminate the program, unwinding
🚽 out of the loop the same way it does from any user-defined function.
🚽
🚽 Before #246 main had no function frame, so `bussin` here neither stopped
🚽 execution nor set the exit code -- it produced "Error: No scope to exit" and,
🚽 without the #319 has_function_frame guard, a four-error cascade. Now interpret()
🚽 runs main under a function jump buffer, so the `bussin` at i == 2 ends the
🚽 program cleanly: "before" prints, the loop stops mid-iteration, "AFTER LOOP"
🚽 never runs, and the process exits 0.
skibidi main {
    yapping("before");
    flex (rizz i = 0; i < 5; i = i + 1) {
        edgy (i == 2) {
            bussin 0;
        }
    }
    yapping("AFTER LOOP");
    bussin 0;
}
